<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>QuantX India | Professional Index & Options Analytics Terminal</title>
  <meta name="description" content="QuantX India is a private trading analytics terminal for Indian index and options markets, using Dhan API market data, professional charting, option-chain intelligence and AI-assisted trade journaling.">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="assets/favicon.png">
  <style>
    :root{
      --bg:#050914;
      --panel:#0b1220;
      --panel2:#0f172a;
      --line:#1e293b;
      --muted:#9fb0c7;
      --text:#e5edf7;
      --cyan:#67e8f9;
      --teal:#5eead4;
      --green:#22c55e;
      --saffron:#f59e0b;
      --blue:#38bdf8;
    }
    *{box-sizing:border-box}
    html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
    body{
      margin:0;
      font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Inter,Arial,sans-serif;
      background:linear-gradient(180deg,#050914 0%,#071020 52%,#050914 100%);
      color:var(--text);
      line-height:1.65;
    }
    a{color:var(--cyan);text-decoration:none}
    a:hover{text-decoration:underline}
    header{
      position:sticky;top:0;z-index:20;
      padding:18px 7%;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.16);
      display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;
      backdrop-filter:blur(16px);
      background:rgba(5,9,20,.82);
    }
    .brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;font-size:22px;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:.3px;color:var(--teal)}
    .brand img{width:46px;height:46px;border-radius:13px;box-shadow:0 0 28px rgba(34,211,238,.22)}
    nav{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:flex-end}
    nav a{color:#cbd5e1;font-size:14px;font-weight:600}
    .hero{
      padding:96px 7% 76px;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 82% 0%, rgba(14,165,233,.35) 0, rgba(14,165,233,.08) 24%, transparent 46%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 15% 10%, rgba(34,197,94,.18) 0, transparent 32%);
    }
    .hero-inner{max-width:1180px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;gap:42px;align-items:center}
    .eyebrow{
      display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;
      border:1px solid rgba(94,234,212,.38);
      color:var(--teal);
      padding:8px 13px;
      border-radius:999px;
      font-size:13px;
      font-weight:800;
      margin-bottom:22px;
      background:rgba(15,118,110,.14);
    }
    .hero h1{font-size:58px;line-height:1.04;margin:0 0 22px;letter-spacing:-1.6px}
    .hero p{font-size:19px;color:#b8c7d9;max-width:790px;margin:0 0 30px}
    .hero-actions{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
    .btn{
      display:inline-block;
      padding:13px 18px;
      border-radius:12px;
      font-weight:800;
      border:1px solid rgba(103,232,249,.28);
      background:#0b375d;
      color:#e0f2fe;
    }
    .btn.secondary{background:rgba(15,23,42,.9);color:#dbeafe;border-color:#334155}
    .terminal-card{
      background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgba(15,23,42,.92),rgba(2,6,23,.92));
      border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.18);
      border-radius:26px;
      padding:26px;
      box-shadow:0 24px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.32);
    }
    .terminal-card img{width:128px;height:128px;border-radius:30px;box-shadow:0 0 58px rgba(34,211,238,.24);display:block;margin:4px auto 26px}
    .metric-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px}
    .metric{background:#08111f;border:1px solid #172033;border-radius:16px;padding:14px}
    .metric b{display:block;color:var(--cyan);font-size:13px}
    .metric span{color:#dbeafe;font-size:18px;font-weight:800}
    section{padding:66px 7%;border-top:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.12)}
    .section-head{max-width:860px;margin-bottom:30px}
    h2{font-size:36px;margin:0 0 14px;letter-spacing:-.7px}
    .lead{color:#aebdd1;font-size:18px;margin:0}
    .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(250px,1fr));gap:18px}
    .card{
      background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(15,23,42,.96),rgba(11,18,32,.96));
      border:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.16);
      border-radius:18px;
      padding:24px;
    }
    .card h3{margin:0 0 10px;color:#dffbff;font-size:19px}
    .card p{color:#aebdd1;margin:0}
    .card .tag{display:inline-block;color:#082f49;background:var(--cyan);padding:4px 8px;border-radius:7px;font-size:12px;font-weight:900;margin-bottom:12px}
    .split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.9fr 1.1fr;gap:28px;align-items:start}
    .list{display:grid;gap:12px}
    .item{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;background:#0b1220;border:1px solid #1e293b;border-radius:16px;padding:16px}
    .dot{width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--green);margin-top:8px;box-shadow:0 0 18px rgba(34,197,94,.6);flex:0 0 auto}
    .symbols{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:18px}
    .symbols span{background:#111827;border:1px solid #253148;color:#dbeafe;padding:8px 12px;border-radius:999px;font-size:13px;font-weight:800}
    .timeline{counter-reset:step;display:grid;gap:14px}
    .step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:16px;background:#0b1220;border:1px solid #1e293b;border-radius:18px;padding:18px}
    .step:before{counter-increment:step;content:counter(step);width:42px;height:42px;border-radius:14px;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#0b375d;color:#e0f2fe;font-weight:900}
    .step h3{margin:0 0 6px}
    .step p{margin:0;color:#aebdd1}
    .notice{background:rgba(245,158,11,.1);border:1px solid rgba(245,158,11,.28);border-radius:18px;padding:20px;color:#fde68a}
    .contact-box{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(14,165,233,.18),rgba(34,197,94,.1));border:1px solid rgba(103,232,249,.24);border-radius:22px;padding:28px}
    footer{padding:34px 7%;color:#8ea0b6;border-top:1px solid #172033;font-size:14px}
    @media(max-width:860px){
      .hero-inner,.split{grid-template-columns:1fr}
      .hero h1{font-size:42px}
      header{align-items:flex-start;gap:14px;flex-direction:column}
      nav{justify-content:flex-start}
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <div class="brand"><img src="assets/quantx-logo.png" alt="QuantX India logo"><span>QuantX India</span></div>
    <nav>
      <a href="#product">Product</a>
      <a href="#datafeed">Datafeed</a>
      <a href="#analytics">Analytics</a>
      <a href="#tradingview">TradingView</a>
      <a href="#roadmap">Roadmap</a>
      <a href="privacy.html">Privacy</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Private trading analytics terminal · India markets</div>
          <h1>Professional charting and options intelligence for Indian index traders.</h1>
          <p>
            QuantX India is a private desktop/web trading analytics terminal being developed for Indian index
            and options markets. The platform combines broker API market data, multi-index charting,
            option-chain analytics, risk tools, strategy research and AI-assisted trade review into one
            focused workflow.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn" href="#tradingview">TradingView integration purpose</a>
            <a class="btn secondary" href="#datafeed">View datafeed architecture</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="terminal-card">
          <img src="assets/quantx-logo.png" alt="QuantX India symbol">
          <div class="metric-grid">
            <div class="metric"><b>Markets</b><span>Index & Options</span></div>
            <div class="metric"><b>Datafeed</b><span>Dhan API</span></div>
            <div class="metric"><b>Mode</b><span>Private Terminal</span></div>
            <div class="metric"><b>Focus</b><span>Risk + Analytics</span></div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="product">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Product overview</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          QuantX India is designed as a professional research and execution-support terminal for a trader
          who needs fast market context, clean charts and structured option-chain intelligence.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="tag">Charts</span>
          <h3>Live OHLC market visualisation</h3>
          <p>Multi-timeframe candlestick charts, volume, zoom controls, position lock, symbol switching and chart-state stability for Indian index instruments.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="tag">Options</span>
          <h3>Option-chain intelligence</h3>
          <p>Option-chain snapshots, PCR, Max Pain, open-interest changes, strike-level support/resistance and market summary panels.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="tag">Risk</span>
          <h3>Strategy and risk workflow</h3>
          <p>Greeks, implied volatility, payoff modelling, strategy builder, backtesting, bracket-order planning and trade lifecycle review.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="tag">AI</span>
          <h3>AI-assisted trade journal</h3>
          <p>Structured post-trade explanations, market condition notes, decision-quality review and performance feedback for continuous improvement.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="datafeed">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>Own datafeed architecture</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            QuantX India is built around a local backend and broker API integration. The charting layer is intended
            to consume our own market-data endpoints rather than relying on public embed widgets.
          </p>
          <div class="symbols">
            <span>NIFTY</span><span>BANKNIFTY</span><span>FINNIFTY</span><span>MIDCPNIFTY</span><span>SENSEX</span><span>BANKEX</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="list">
          <div class="item"><span class="dot"></span><div><b>Dhan API market feed</b><br><span class="lead">Used for historical OHLC candles, option-chain data and market snapshots.</span></div></div>
          <div class="item"><span class="dot"></span><div><b>Local FastAPI backend</b><br><span class="lead">Serves chart data, analytics and terminal UI to a private macOS/web interface.</span></div></div>
          <div class="item"><span class="dot"></span><div><b>Multi-index symbol resolver</b><br><span class="lead">Maps supported index instruments to backend data endpoints and chart symbols.</span></div></div>
          <div class="item"><span class="dot"></span><div><b>Rate-limit aware design</b><br><span class="lead">Uses caching, controlled refresh and policy guards for broker API stability.</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="analytics">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Analytics modules</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          The platform is structured as a modular analytics system, so charting, options, risk and journal tools can
          work together without becoming a simple standalone chart page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card"><h3>Market structure</h3><p>Trend context, multi-timeframe candles, volume, support/resistance and market regime labelling.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Options intelligence</h3><p>PCR, Max Pain, OI buildup, strike concentration, option-chain dashboard and snapshot comparisons.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Pricing and Greeks</h3><p>Black-Scholes, Greeks, implied volatility, expiry sensitivity and risk-factor explanation for option positions.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Strategy research</h3><p>Payoff diagrams, strategy builder, backtesting logic, bracket order planning and risk-reward templates.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Performance review</h3><p>Trade history, journal output, behavioural notes, performance statistics and post-trade AI explanation.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Export/reporting</h3><p>Trade tickets, reports, Excel-compatible exports and structured audit logs for review.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="tradingview">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>TradingView charting integration purpose</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          QuantX India is requesting TradingView charting access to upgrade the terminal from an internal chart
          renderer to a professional-grade charting experience with advanced layouts, indicators and drawing tools.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Why TradingView</h3>
          <p>TradingView-style professional charting is central to the product experience: smooth candles, clean scaling, indicators, drawings, layouts and chart-state persistence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>How it will be used</h3>
          <p>The library will be hosted inside QuantX India's private terminal and connected to our own backend datafeed for Indian market instruments.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Not a public widget clone</h3>
          <p>The project is not intended as a public chart-embedding page. It is a private analytics terminal with broker-data integration and options workflow tools.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="notice" style="margin-top:22px">
        QuantX India is private trading analytics software. It is not investment advice, portfolio management, or a public brokerage service.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="roadmap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Development roadmap</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          The current architecture is designed for staged development, where charting, datafeed, analytics and trading workflow modules are integrated progressively.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="step"><div><h3>Charting and datafeed foundation</h3><p>Multi-index OHLC feed, option-chain data, local backend, frontend chart shell and stable terminal launcher.</p></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div><h3>Professional charting upgrade</h3><p>TradingView library integration, symbol resolver, real-time bar updates, saved layouts and drawing persistence.</p></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div><h3>Options analytics expansion</h3><p>Greeks, IV, OI analysis, max pain, PCR, strategy builder and payoff modelling.</p></div></div>
        <div class="step"><div><h3>Trading workflow and review</h3><p>Bracket-order planning, risk templates, trade lifecycle tracking, AI journal and performance dashboard.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <div class="contact-box">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Rishabh Singh<br>
          Founder / Developer, QuantX India<br>
          <a href="mailto:rishabh@quantx-india.com">rishabh@quantx-india.com</a><br>
          GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/rishabh82cs-ai">github.com/rishabh82cs-ai</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    © 2026 QuantX India. Private trading analytics software for research and workflow support.
    Not investment advice. · <a href="privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="terms.html">Terms</a>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
